{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1521353-a-post-apocalyptic-setting-for-hunter-the-reckoning","id":1521353,"title":"A Post-Apocalyptic Setting for Hunter: the Reckoning","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-24T15:42:08-07:00","id":1521353,"title":"A Post-Apocalyptic Setting for Hunter: the Reckoning","content":"This setting is a basic Golden Age Sci Fi Post-apocalyptic setting. In this case a plague wiped out 95% of Humanity. The Wererats, allied with the Red Talons summoned the plague. <br /> <br /> Before finding out the Rat shifters and the Red Talons were responsible, the Mages of many factions allied with the Changelings destroyed the vast majority of the Nephandi and their Sabbat and Black Spiral Dancer allies. <br /> <br /> None of this restores civilization. The Changelings have gone into slumber for a few generations. The Mages created bases to both teach new Mages and to preserve and revive civilization. But the Mages needed allies. They chose the Hunters. It's worked out better than you'd think. <br /> <br /> Now the Hunters are hunting again. Disguised as peddlers and other commercial travelers, the Hunters both fight the monsters and help rekindle civilization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T15:51:52-07:00","id":1521354,"title":"","content":"The Mages provide the Hunters with trade goods, means of transport, and professional training. Traveling doctors, Nurse-Praticioners, Dentists, Opticians, and others are always welcome. The Mages train the Hunters in these skills. Many a <b>JUDGE </b> is now the &quot;Circut Judge.&quot; The Mages successfully conning many people into excepting the authority of such Judges. However, peddlers are the most common disguise. <br /> <br /> The mages seek to help these chaotic poorly formed communities survive. Providing useful tools and knowledge and defending these communities from predators is a key part of the plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T15:57:45-07:00","id":1521355,"title":"","content":"Feel free to kibitz. I'm going to post more ideas later.<br /> <br /> Although most technology doesn't work in this world (largely because the systems that supported modern civilization are gone or neglected, if no one runs the power plant, no one gets electricity). Many things like car tires have been worn out or rotted. There are surviving pieces of useful technology. The Mages and their allies are trying to rebuild civilization with the available resources and appropriate technologies. <br /> <br /> People will need to both relearn basic survival skills and survive climate change. Which, even with the near total collapse of fossil fuel use, is still ongoing. Reteaching humanity is a priority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-24-2023, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T01:42:54-07:00","id":1521365,"title":"","content":"The most common supernaturals that the PC Hunters will be in conflict with are <b>Wrights </b>and corpses animated by either magic (<b>Zombies)</b> or Wraiths (<b>Revenants).</b><br /> <br /> Wrights are discussed in the Vampire book <b>Sins of the Blood. </b>Basically, when a Cannite Vampire goes to zero Humanity they become a Wright.<br /> <br /> Wrights are basically cunning animals in human form. Most higher brain functions like language are gone. Empathy exists only as a predator analyzing its prey. Wrights still have all the vulnerabilities of Vampires and new ones too. Holy symbols from the culture the Wright was raised in terrify Wrights. Garlic repulses Wrights. Like many supernatural creatures of folklore, Wrights are normally obsessive compulsive. Throwing down a handful of small objects like seeds or stick pins can often distract a Wright who will obsessively count the lot.<br /> <br /> Wrights generally have the disciplines of <b>Potence, Celerity, </b>and <b>Fortitude </b>but rarely at high degrees. It isn't rare for Wrights to have the lower levels of <b>Auspex, Obfuscation, Protean, Animalism, Presance, </b>and <b>Domination. </b>But the higher levels require creative thought, and aren't possible for a Wright. <b>Thaumuturgy </b>and the other special powers of most obscure clans and Bloodlines require to much of a wright's brain for them to be used. The one exception is <b>Melpominee. </b>Perhaps music is simply more basic than most people think. However, the Daughters of Concaphaney are very rare.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-25-2023, 04:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-26T15:23:56-07:00","id":1521446,"title":"","content":"<b>Zombies </b>and <b>Revenants </b>seem similar but they are different threats. <b>Zombies </b>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bseem to be animated by the chaotic forces released by the plague. They are shambling mindless corpses hungry for the flesh of the living. They rot slowly over time and few new <b>Zombies </b>have been created in decades. They are now rare. But the outbreaks are still terrifying. <br /> <br /> <b>Revenants </b>are animated by Wraiths and occasionally Spectors. <b>Revenants </b>rot far more quickly than <b>Zombies </b>but with the various powers of Wraiths, they can sometimes pass for human, if only for a short time. <b>Revenants </b>have the intelligence and purposes of the Wraiths or Spectors that animate them. <br /> <br /> <b>Risen </b>\u200b\u200bdo exist in this setting, but they are, as always, very rare. <br /> <br /> <b>Wrights </b>can occasionally embrace a mortal turning them into Vampires. These are always weak Vampires with low humanity and little understanding of their powers. Most end up as <b>Wrights. </b>Although a tiny minority to advance and become more powerful and skilled. <br /> <br /> <b>Vampires </b>have survived, but very few. Most are in Topor waiting for better times. But a few are building up their powerbase. Hunters are determined to break these.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-26T15:31:18-07:00","id":1521447,"title":"","content":"I'll describe the conditions of each of the major supernatural groups.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampires : </b>Neither the Camarilla nor the Sabbat still exist in any real sense. The conditions of other smaller groups like the Black Hand or the Independent Clans aren't known or, given the conditions of this world knowable.<br /> <br /> All known Vampire\u2077s are trying to build up some kind of secure powerbase. They are both paranoid and generally sneaky. Watch the old film <b>Vampyr</b>. Look at how Marguerite Chopin (the vampire) manipulates the entire community and rules it from the shadows with a ghoul catspaw. Even powerful Vampires hide in the shadows until they have to strike. <br /> <br /> <b>Garou and Fera:</b> Shattered and in isolation. A few groups, like the Werebears and the Children of Gaia have allied with the Mages. They many work to heal the environment. Some shifters are attacking human communities to limit human population numbers. Most other shifters hate these attacks but do little against them. <br /> <br /> Some <b>Garou </b>hunt Hunters in order to weaken humanity. <br /> <br /> <b>Wraiths: </b>The Shadowlands are in chaos. Vast storms have dominated the realms of the dead since the plague. A few places are somehow sheltered from the storms gather what <b>Wraiths </b>are near. These places tend to be the kinds of large buildings that attract ghost legends (read <b>Ghostlands </b>there is a type of building that attracts ghost stories even if they lack ghosts). <br /> <br /> <b>Risen </b>in this world are sometimes just escaping the horror of these storms.<br /> <br /> <b>Changelings: </b>The Changelings and related creatures are almost all withdrawn from the world. A few <b>Changelings </b>are still around, these are always working with the mages.<br /> <br /> <b>Mages:</b> The Council of the Traditions is radically changed but still around. Several other groups have joined the Council (Now the Council of Seventeen, referencing West African numerology) and are mainly working for base survival. Some groups have become serious threats. <br /> <br /> more later","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-26-2023, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T15:23:21-07:00","id":1521547,"title":"","content":"Mages are working under altered conditions. With such a low world population <b>Paradox </b>is massively weakened. Everywhere on Earth <b>Magick </b>is either <b>Coincidental </b>or <b>Uncanny </b>(to steal a cool term from <b>Victorian Mage </b>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b). Difficulties for performing <b>Magick </b>is about as it was before the year 1000AD. (later on I'll post the book were these lower levels are stated).<br /> <br /> A further benefit that effects both <b>Mages </b>and <b>Hunters </b>is slowed aging. Mages find their aging is slowed by the square of their <b>Arete</b>. Thus an <b>Arete </b>2 Mage ages at one quarter the rate of <b>Sleepers</b>. <b>\u200bArete </b>4 <b>Mages </b>age at on sixteenth the rate of <b>Sleepers</b>. <b>Hunters </b>age at one third the rate of ordinary people.<br /> <br /> On the downside, <b>Quintessence </b>is far rarer. Many <b>Nodes </b>have either lowered their level or gone dormant. Although not all <b>Nodes </b>or <b>Caerns </b>have been affected. It's dramatically harder for <b>Mages </b>to increase <b>Arete </b>or increase or learn new <b>Spheres. </b><br /> <br /> Several powerful Mages say it's as if the world was numb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-30-2023, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T15:38:17-07:00","id":1521549,"title":"","content":"<b>Hunters </b>basically hide in plain sight in order to hunt the monsters. There are powerful threats that want to forbid all outside contact. However, the <b>Hunters </b>are bringing useful services and goods.<br /> <br /> For example, it's one thing to figure out how to sew. Try making needles. In most places clothing is extremely useful for survival. Cloth, thread, sewing tools, looms, spinning wheels, carding combs, and more are sold by the <b>Hunters</b>. Multiply this through dozens of common needs.<br /> <br /> The monsters, if they need to keep people under control, can't shut out the <b>Hunters</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-30-2023, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T16:19:31-07:00","id":1521552,"title":"","content":"Others can chime in with their ideas and/or objections. <br /> <br /> Do you like the idea? How are you going to change it for your campaign? Who do you think would make a tasty antagonist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T09:08:59-07:00","id":1521667,"title":"","content":"I like it, I'd like to see where the fallen end up in there and I think it'd be cool to have a council of powerful(ish) supes that are trying to fix things and reverse the &quot;apocalypse&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T07:54:12-07:00","id":1522097,"title":"","content":"I think it could be a cool setting to play regular humans. For survival-horror stories. Trying to survive, hearing about these mage controled places as legend and paradises to search for, &quot;Atlantis&quot;-like, but also having predatory supers that would take advantage on them as a scary factor.<br /> <br /> Maybe getting the Imbuing after a couple of sessions, when/if base survival starts growing old (Not that Imbued would have an easy time, but to have a &quot;calling&quot;, to ally with the mages, to start working towards &quot;grander scale&quot; plans ... it's all more hopeful stuff).<br /> <br /> *For Mages:<br /> <br /> I would make Mages only have an easy time with Paradox within these special places where they've &quot;restored society&quot;. The rest of the world would have &quot;desolation/despair&quot; as &quot;Reality Zone&quot;, caused by the horror of the Apocalypse as it literally &quot;sunk in&quot; - for a more apolcaliptic feel. It would make mages more issolated, and adds another layer of complexity to the problem of rebuilding society, where they *have* to make some places feel secure to better work their miracles.<br /> <br /> Also it goes well with both Mage placing a great importance on Reality Zones and building belief, and with Hunter take on mages as &quot;manipulators&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Council would try to build techno-mystic places (to avoid infigthing), but looners and extremists could try to build &quot;their own&quot;, manipulating communities into following their Focus<br /> <br /> Vitae it's a source of Quintessence (albeit one very corrupt source). Some Mages (especially those of darker pursues) could consider allying with vampires to create their own small &quot;new carthague&quot;'s, of varied levels of horror.<br /> <br /> *For the Imbued: the Messengers may need to change their tune a little <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> , pointing at the supernatural and shouting &quot;unclean monsters&quot; it's <i>not </i>conducent to ease cooperation between Imbued and other Supers, so it would be better if they ease their position on non-humans a little (or, like, a lot) :P<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-05-2023, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T11:42:47-07:00","id":1522110,"title":"","content":"This would be survival horror for regular humans. Outside of the Mage enclaves people live, in most ways, like they did in the American frontier in the 1760-1800 period. The &quot;peddlers&quot; make small differences. Radios, push-peddle sewing machines, vaccines, a wider variety of garden vegetables, but life is still fragile and isolated. Wrights, dark mages, bandits, Wraiths, all make it a fragile life. <br /> <br /> The Mages are lighting lamps. The Hunters are trying to keep them lit. &quot;But however fast the light travels, it finds the darkness there ahead of it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}